<title>FRANCE: Total sees oil price below $20/barrel.</title>
<headline>Total sees oil price below $20/barrel.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>French oil company Total SA expects the price of Brent crude oil to return to below $20 per barrel, chairman Thierry Desmarest told the Journal des Finances weekly.</p>
<p>&quot;In 1997, there will be a rather substantial re-adjustment, without doubt to below 20 dollars per barrel,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>&quot;Stocks are at their lows. The rate at which they will be replenished is decisive,&quot; he said, adding that Total's investments would remain profitable with a crude price of $16 barrels per share.</p>
</text>
